2. Recommended Commercial Model 
I'd avoid making this complicated initially. 
90-Day Pilot 
No upfront integration fee. 
Cyber Fleet Services receives qualified opportunities generated through RoboReady. 
RoboReady receives: 
● $500 per qualified lead accepted by Cyber Fleet Services 
● $2,500 when a lead advances to a formal site-development opportunity 

● 2% of Cyber Fleet Services' net site revenue for successfully deployed 
RoboReady-originated locations 
Those numbers are proposed starting points, not claims about Cyber Fleet Services' 
existing economics. 
After 90 days, both parties review: 
● Number of properties assessed 
● Qualified leads 
● Site evaluations 
● Agreements signed 
● Deployments 
● Revenue generated 
● Conversion rates 
Then move to a longer-term agreement. 
 
3. The Proposal to Cyber Fleet Services 
Below is the version I'd actually send. 
RoboReady × Cyber Fleet Services Strategic Partnership Proposal 
Strategic Partnership Proposal 
RoboReady × Cyber Fleet Services 
Property Intelligence → Site Qualification → Fleet Deployment 
Prepared for: Cyber Fleet Services 
Prepared by: RoboReady 
Proposed structure: 90-Day Pilot Partnership 
 
Executive Summary 
RoboReady proposes a strategic partnership with Cyber Fleet Services to create a 
scalable pipeline of qualified commercial properties suitable for autonomous fleet 
charging, staging, parking and related infrastructure. 
RoboReady's role is to identify, assess and qualify properties before they reach Cyber 
Fleet Services. 
Cyber Fleet Services' role is to evaluate, commercialize and deploy the appropriate fleet 
infrastructure and operating model. 

The objective is simple: 
RoboReady finds and qualifies the sites. Cyber Fleet Services converts qualified sites 
into operating assets. 
This partnership allows Cyber Fleet Services to expand its property pipeline while 
reducing the amount of time and resources required to identify and initially screen 
potential locations. 
 
1. Partnership Opportunity 
The expansion of autonomous mobility requires more than vehicles. 
It requires strategically located physical infrastructure, including: 
● Charging capacity 
● Vehicle staging 
● Parking 
● Fleet access 
● Electrical infrastructure 
● Property access 
● Commercially viable locations 
● Locations capable of supporting future expansion 
Commercial property owners may have suitable real estate but lack the technical 
knowledge to determine whether their property is appropriate for autonomous fleet 
operations. 
RoboReady can serve as the initial property intelligence and qualification layer. 
Cyber Fleet Services can then serve as the commercialization and deployment layer. 
Together, the companies can create a repeatable property-to-deployment pipeline. 
 
2. Proposed Customer Journey 
Step 1 — Property Submission 
A commercial property owner submits a property to RoboReady for evaluation. 
Step 2 — RoboReady Assessment 
RoboReady evaluates the property based on agreed Cyber Fleet Services criteria. 
The assessment can evaluate: 

● Location 
● Parking capacity 
● Vehicle circulation 
● Access 
● Staging potential 
● Charging potential 
● Infrastructure considerations 
● Expansion potential 
● Site constraints 
● Preliminary deployment suitability 
Step 3 — Cyber Fleet Readiness Score 
RoboReady produces a standardized readiness score. 
Example: 
Cyber Fleet Readiness Score: 87 / 100 
The property is categorized as: 
● Deployment Candidate 
● Further Evaluation Required 
● Not Currently Recommended 
Step 4 — Qualified Lead Handoff 
Properties meeting the agreed qualification criteria are presented to Cyber Fleet 
Services. 
Cyber Fleet Services receives the relevant property and assessment information 
required for its next-stage review. 
Step 5 — Cyber Fleet Services Evaluation 
Cyber Fleet Services determines whether to: 
● Accept the opportunity 
● Request additional information 
● Conduct a site evaluation 
● Enter commercial discussions 
● Decline the opportunity 
Step 6 — Commercialization 
If appropriate, Cyber Fleet Services proceeds with its normal process for property 
agreements, infrastructure deployment and fleet operations. 
Step 7 — Revenue Attribution 

RoboReady-originated opportunities are tracked through the partnership so both 
companies can measure: 
● Leads 
● Qualified properties 
● Site evaluations 
● Agreements 
● Deployments 
● Revenue 
 
3. Proposed Pilot Program 
We recommend beginning with a 90-day pilot. 
Pilot objectives 
The pilot will determine whether RoboReady can efficiently generate qualified property 
opportunities for Cyber Fleet Services. 
The initial target would be: 
25–50 assessed properties 
with a goal of generating a meaningful number of qualified opportunities for Cyber Fleet 
Services review. 
During the pilot, the companies will establish: 
1. Property qualification criteria 
2. Geographic priorities 
3. Minimum site requirements 
4. Lead acceptance criteria 
5. Data-sharing procedures 
6. Lead handoff process 
7. Revenue attribution 
8. Performance metrics 
 
4. Roles & Responsibilities 
RoboReady 
RoboReady will: 
● Identify potential commercial properties 
● Conduct initial site assessments 

● Apply agreed qualification criteria 
● Produce readiness scores 
● Generate property assessment reports 
● Identify qualified opportunities 
● Introduce qualified property owners to Cyber Fleet Services 
● Track lead status and attribution 
● Provide reporting during the pilot 
Cyber Fleet Services 
Cyber Fleet Services will: 
● Define target site characteristics 
● Provide technical and commercial qualification criteria 
● Review qualified RoboReady opportunities 
● Determine which opportunities warrant further evaluation 
● Conduct its normal commercial and technical diligence 
● Negotiate property agreements where appropriate 
● Manage deployment and operations 
● Provide status updates necessary to measure partnership performance 
Joint Responsibilities 
Both companies will: 
● Establish a standardized qualification framework 
● Review pilot performance 
● Improve conversion rates 
● Develop joint marketing opportunities 
● Determine long-term commercial terms 
 
5. Proposed Commercial Structure 
For the initial pilot, RoboReady proposes the following framework: 
Qualified Lead Fee 
$500 per qualified property accepted by Cyber Fleet Services. 
A qualified lead would meet mutually agreed site criteria and contain sufficient 
information for Cyber Fleet Services to conduct an initial evaluation. 
Development Opportunity Fee 
$2,500 per RoboReady-originated property that advances to a formal site-development 
opportunity. 
Deployment Revenue Share 

For properties that ultimately become operational Cyber Fleet Services locations: 
2% of net site revenue attributable to the deployed location for an agreed period. 
The parties may modify these economics following the pilot based on actual conversion 
rates and site economics. 
 
6. Alternative Commercial Model 
If Cyber Fleet Services prefers a simpler structure, the parties could instead use a 
single success-based model. 
For example: 
RoboReady receives compensation only when a RoboReady-originated property 
reaches a defined commercial milestone. 
This could be structured as: 
● Site evaluation completed 
● Property agreement executed 
● Deployment completed 
The final economics can be determined after the initial pilot produces real conversion 
data. 
 
7. Cyber Fleet Ready™ 
As part of the partnership, RoboReady proposes developing a dedicated: 
Cyber Fleet Ready™ Score 
The score would provide a standardized way to evaluate properties against Cyber Fleet 
Services' requirements. 
Potential scoring categories include: 
Category Example Weight 
Location 15% 

Site access 15% 
Staging capacity 15% 
Charging potential 20% 
Electrical/infrastructure potential 15% 
Traffic/vehicle circulation 10% 
Expansion potential 10% 
The final scoring methodology would be developed jointly with Cyber Fleet Services. 
This creates a repeatable qualification standard that can improve as more sites are 
evaluated. 
 
8. Technology & Lead Handoff 
The intended workflow is: 
Property Owner 
↓ 
RoboReady 
↓ 
Assessment 
↓ 
Cyber Fleet Ready™ Score 
↓ 

Qualified Opportunity 
↓ 
Cyber Fleet Services 
↓ 
Site Evaluation 
↓ 
