↓ 
Deployment 
↓ 
Operating Revenue 
RoboReady will maintain attribution for properties originating through the RoboReady 
platform so that commercial outcomes can be measured accurately. 
 
9. Pilot Metrics 
At the conclusion of the 90-day pilot, the companies will review: 
● Number of properties submitted 
● Number assessed 
● Number meeting qualification criteria 
● Number accepted by Cyber Fleet Services 
● Number receiving site evaluations 
● Number entering commercial negotiations 
● Number of agreements executed 
● Number of deployments 
● Estimated pipeline value 
● Actual revenue generated 
● Cost per qualified opportunity 
● Conversion rate 
The goal is to establish a measurable acquisition channel rather than simply generate 
unqualified leads. 

 
10. Long-Term Opportunity 
If the pilot demonstrates strong results, the partnership can expand beyond referrals. 
Potential future initiatives include: 
White-Label Site Assessment 
Cyber Fleet Services could offer RoboReady assessments directly as part of its property 
acquisition process. 
Joint Property Acquisition 
The companies could jointly target: 
● Parking operators 
● Shopping centers 
● Hotels 
● Multifamily properties 
● Commercial real estate owners 
● Fleet facilities 
● Existing charging locations 
● Strategic transportation locations 
Property Marketplace 
RoboReady could create a marketplace of pre-qualified autonomous mobility properties 
available for review by Cyber Fleet Services and other qualified operators. 
Portfolio Assessment 
Large property owners could have entire portfolios evaluated and ranked for 
autonomous fleet infrastructure potential. 
This would allow a single commercial relationship to generate multiple potential 
deployment locations. 
 
11. Why This Partnership Makes Sense 
Cyber Fleet Services brings the operational and commercialization capability required to 
turn suitable properties into functioning fleet infrastructure. 
RoboReady brings the property intelligence, assessment and qualification capability 
required to identify those properties. 
The combined value proposition is: 

Identify the right properties faster, qualify them earlier, and move the best opportunities 
into deployment. 
This creates a scalable acquisition engine for autonomous mobility infrastructure. 
 
12. Proposed Next Steps 
RoboReady proposes a working session between the two teams to finalize: 
1. Target geography 
2. Property types 
3. Minimum site requirements 
4. Technical qualification criteria 
5. Cyber Fleet Ready™ scoring methodology 
6. Lead handoff process 
7. Pilot economics 
8. Data-sharing requirements 
9. 90-day pilot launch date 
Following that meeting, RoboReady can configure the assessment and begin 
generating the first qualified property opportunities. 
 
Proposed Partnership 
RoboReady: Property intelligence, assessment and qualification 
