4. What I'd do next 
I would not send the proposal and wait. 
I'd turn this into a three-step sales process: 
Step 1 — Send the proposal 

Ask for a 30-minute partnership call, not a generic “let us know what you think.” 
Step 2 — On the call, get their criteria 
The most important thing to extract from Cyber Fleet Services is their actual definition of 
a good site: 
“Give us the top 10 characteristics of a property you would want us to see.” 
That information becomes RoboReady's scoring algorithm. 
Step 3 — Come back with a live demonstration 
Show them something tangible: 
“Here are 10 properties RoboReady identified. Here is the Cyber Fleet Ready score for 
each. Here are the 3 we'd recommend your team contact first.” 
That changes the conversation from “partnership idea” to “here's your pipeline.” 
If you want, I can also turn this into a polished 8–10 slide investor/partner pitch deck for 
RoboReady → Cyber Fleet Services, including the visual process flow, revenue model, 
pilot economics, and exact slides to present to their CEO/business-development team. 
 